From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TinyYana <yanasakuranight@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 19:46:17 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Lophinya: folia-supported gate defaults open (run any Paper
 plugin)

Lophine/Folia refuses to load any jar that does not declare folia-supported.
That is the plugin author's one-time self-report, not a runtime safety
mechanism - region ownership checking is, and it is untouched here.

Lophinya exists to run any Paper plugin on top of Lophine, so this gate now
defaults to open: an undeclared jar loads, and if it genuinely cannot work
under regionised threading it throws at the actual callsite, with patch 0024's
diagnostics naming the plugin, jar and callsite.

This is not disable_check_for_folia_supported. A tiny SHA-256 deny-list still
refuses jars whose own canonical upstream documents data loss under Folia
(FastAsyncWorldEdit, EssentialsX and its two bundled companions) - that failure
is silent, so letting them run and throw would protect nothing. Adding a plugin
to the server needs no change to this file; only proving one destroys data does.

Kill switch: -Dlophinya.compat.foliaSupportedAllowlist=false restores the stock
Folia gate.

diff --git a/src/main/java/fun/bm/lophinya/compat/LophinyaFoliaSupportedGate.java b/src/main/java/fun/bm/lophinya/compat/LophinyaFoliaSupportedGate.java
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..9ef65000b66eb43bc40a2c87cd717795e9185a1d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/main/java/fun/bm/lophinya/compat/LophinyaFoliaSupportedGate.java
@@ -0,0 +1,145 @@
+package fun.bm.lophinya.compat;
+
+import com.mojang.logging.LogUtils;
+import org.slf4j.Logger;
+
+import java.nio.file.Files;
+import java.nio.file.Path;
+import java.security.MessageDigest;
+import java.util.HexFormat;
+import java.util.Map;
+import java.util.Set;
+import java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;
+
+/**
+ * Lophinya: the {@code folia-supported} load gate, inverted.
+ *
+ * <p>Folia's plugin loader rejects any jar that doesn't declare {@code folia-supported: true} in
+ * its own manifest, before {@code onEnable()} ever runs. That declaration is the plugin's own
+ * one-time self-report, read once at load time - it is <b>not</b> a runtime safety mechanism.
+ * The real safety mechanism is region ownership checking ({@code TickThread.ensureTickThread}),
+ * which runs on every Bukkit world-state access regardless of what a plugin's {@code plugin.yml}
+ * says, and is completely untouched by this class.
+ *
+ * <p>Lophinya's whole reason to exist is to be a layer on top of Lophine that runs <b>any</b> Paper
+ * plugin. Gating that on each plugin author having happened to type one line into their own
+ * {@code plugin.yml} is not compatibility work - it just moves the decision to someone who never
+ * tested against this server. So the gate defaults to <b>open</b>: a jar that does not declare
+ * {@code folia-supported} still loads, and if it genuinely cannot work under regionised threading
+ * it fails the way any incompatibility should - by throwing, loudly, at the actual call, with
+ * {@link LophinyaSchedulerDiagnostics} naming the plugin, the jar and the callsite.
+ *
+ * <p><b>This is not the same thing as Luminol's {@code disable_check_for_folia_supported}</b>, and
+ * the difference is the deny-list below. That flag is an unconditional global bypass. This gate
+ * still refuses a jar whose <b>own canonical upstream documents data loss</b> under Folia - the one
+ * failure mode "it will just throw" does not protect against, because those plugins do not throw,
+ * they silently corrupt. Data safety is priority 1 in PROJECT_CHARTER section 4; "runs any Paper plugin"
+ * is priority 2. The deny-list is where those two meet, and it is deliberately tiny.
+ *
+ * <p>Adding a plugin to this server therefore needs <b>no change to this file</b>. Only the
+ * opposite - establishing that some exact artifact destroys data - does.
+ *
+ * <p>Kill switch: {@code -Dlophinya.compat.foliaSupportedAllowlist=false}. When disabled, every jar
+ * goes back through the stock Folia gate: undeclared jars are rejected at load, as on stock Folia.
+ */
+public final class LophinyaFoliaSupportedGate {
+
+    private static final Logger LOGGER = LogUtils.getLogger();
+
+    public static final boolean ENABLED =
+        !"false".equalsIgnoreCase(System.getProperty("lophinya.compat.foliaSupportedAllowlist", "true"));
+
+    /**
+     * SHA-256 (uppercase hex, no separators) of jars that must <b>not</b> be loaded under Folia even
+     * though the gate is otherwise open, mapped to the reason. The bar for an entry here is high and
+     * specific: the plugin's own canonical upstream states that running it on Folia loses or
+     * corrupts data. Not "untested", not "looks risky", not "no official Folia build" - those all
+     * load, and throw if they must.
+     *
+     * <p>One entry per (plugin, exact version) pair. A version bump changes the hash and drops out
+     * of this list automatically, which is the correct default: a new release may well have fixed
+     * it, and the burden is on evidence, not on inheritance.
+     */
+    private static final Map<String, String> DENY = Map.of(
+        // FastAsyncWorldEdit 2.15.3+1704422 (s01-installed version). Canonical upstream
+        // (IntellectualSites/FastAsyncWorldEdit) PR #2682 states, for Folia, "expect to lose
+        // (world) data". World data loss is silent and unrecoverable - it does not surface as an
+        // exception, so the "let it throw" model gives no protection here.
+        // See project-docs DECISIONS.md D-13 / PLUGIN_INVENTORY.md #8.
+        "D72941FBFFFA8F3E7BF29F5B94AC29BCB20DD042B2AB2E5DBFB06AC12AFA456A", "FastAsyncWorldEdit 2.15.3 (upstream: expect to lose world data on Folia)",
+        // EssentialsX 2.22.1-dev+12 and its two bundled companions (s01-installed versions).
+        // Official EssentialsX has a documented data-loss risk under Folia (project-docs
+        // RISK_REGISTER.md R-05; upstream Folia support PR #6586 still open/unmerged). Same
+        // reasoning as FAWE: the failure mode is lost userdata, not an exception.
+        "ED0C4432BB286CE06820BA5A162FFAC91E34E02EBA644CFCF66AEC4FDA86AF42", "EssentialsX 2.22.1-dev+12 (RISK_REGISTER R-05: userdata loss risk on Folia)",
+        "E41DE7858E2C8F051D69B732D6334BD2D7042DAEB083E772064503AF58A38C6D", "EssentialsXChat 2.22.1-dev+12 (bundled with EssentialsX, same upstream)",
+        "1DF09DA6014F891E0C9A3785C15052B28AB0436CBD3E8EB2D3EF61A99BB32CDA", "EssentialsXSpawn 2.22.1-dev+12 (bundled with EssentialsX, same upstream)"
+    );
+
+    /** SHA-256 of a jar is stable for the run; hashing it on every plugin-load check is wasteful. */
+    private static final Map<Path, String> SHA_CACHE = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
+
+    /** Log the decision once per jar, not once per gate (there are two gates per plugin). */
+    private static final Set<String> LOGGED = ConcurrentHashMap.newKeySet();
+
+    private LophinyaFoliaSupportedGate() {
+    }
+
+    /**
+     * Called only for jars that did <b>not</b> declare {@code folia-supported: true}; jars that did
+     * never reach here.
+     *
+     * @param jarPath path to the plugin jar being loaded
+     * @return true to load it anyway, false to let the stock Folia gate reject it
+     */
+    public static boolean isAllowed(final Path jarPath) {
+        if (!ENABLED || jarPath == null) {
+            return false;
+        }
+        final String sha256;
+        try {
+            sha256 = SHA_CACHE.computeIfAbsent(jarPath, LophinyaFoliaSupportedGate::hash);
+        } catch (final Throwable t) {
+            // Cannot hash it => cannot check it against DENY => must not let it through. This is
+            // the one place the open gate closes on error, and it has to: the deny-list is the
+            // only thing standing between a known data-destroying jar and the world files.
+            LOGGER.warn("[Lophinya] could not hash {} to check it against the folia-supported "
+                + "deny-list; refusing to load it rather than skipping the check", jarPath, t);
+            return false;
+        }
+
+        final String denyReason = DENY.get(sha256);
+        if (denyReason != null) {
+            if (LOGGED.add(sha256)) {
+                LOGGER.error("[Lophinya] REFUSING to load {} - {}. Lophinya loads any Paper plugin "
+                    + "that merely lacks a folia-supported declaration, but not one whose own "
+                    + "upstream documents data loss under Folia: that failure is silent, so letting "
+                    + "it run and throw would protect nothing. Remove the jar or use the Paper "
+                    + "server for this feature.", jarPath.getFileName(), denyReason);
+            }
+            return false;
+        }
+
+        if (LOGGED.add(sha256)) {
+            // Deliberately says nothing about whether this jar declared folia-supported: one of the
+            // three call sites (SpigotPluginProvider, legacy enable-time path) consults this gate
+            // for every legacy plugin, declared or not, so claiming "does not declare" here would
+            // be false for jars that do.
+            LOGGER.info("[Lophinya] folia-supported gate open for {} - Lophinya runs any Paper "
+                + "plugin. Region ownership checks (TickThread.ensureTickThread) are unaffected and "
+                + "still apply to every world-state call it makes; if it cannot work here it throws "
+                + "at the callsite, with diagnostics.", jarPath.getFileName());
+        }
+        return true;
+    }
+
+    private static String hash(final Path jarPath) {
+        try {
+            final MessageDigest md = MessageDigest.getInstance("SHA-256");
+            return HexFormat.of().withUpperCase().formatHex(md.digest(Files.readAllBytes(jarPath)));
+        } catch (final Throwable t) {
+            // Rethrown so isAllowed() fails closed - returning a sentinel would silently miss DENY.
+            throw new RuntimeException("cannot hash " + jarPath, t);
+        }
+    }
+}
diff --git a/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/plugin/provider/type/paper/PaperPluginProviderFactory.java b/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/plugin/provider/type/paper/PaperPluginProviderFactory.java
index c20c04938b2f62b9e75831c5fdfabbd6ec51538a..b5632b317a29da80fefaae074629e8d97b3e03a6 100644
--- a/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/plugin/provider/type/paper/PaperPluginProviderFactory.java
+++ b/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/plugin/provider/type/paper/PaperPluginProviderFactory.java
@@ -25,7 +25,8 @@ class PaperPluginProviderFactory implements PluginTypeFactory<PaperPluginParent,
     @Override
     public PaperPluginParent build(JarFile file, PaperPluginMeta configuration, Path source) {
         // Folia start - block plugins not marked as supported
-        if (!configuration.isFoliaSupported() && !me.earthme.luminol.config.modules.unsupported.DisableCheckForFoliaSupported.disableForPaper) { // Luminol - disable check for folia supported
+        if (!configuration.isFoliaSupported() && !me.earthme.luminol.config.modules.unsupported.DisableCheckForFoliaSupported.disableForPaper
+            && !fun.bm.lophinya.compat.LophinyaFoliaSupportedGate.isAllowed(source)) { // Lophinya - folia-supported gate defaults open
             throw new RuntimeException("Could not load plugin '" + configuration.getDisplayName() + "' as it is not marked as supporting Folia!");
         }
         // Folia end - block plugins not marked as supported
diff --git a/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/plugin/provider/type/spigot/SpigotPluginProvider.java b/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/plugin/provider/type/spigot/SpigotPluginProvider.java
index 0fd1040ed376f19c6d5326767baaf3048ce1bfb4..b5560729fe6d494f5420610497b5ee548b205ea0 100644
--- a/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/plugin/provider/type/spigot/SpigotPluginProvider.java
+++ b/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/plugin/provider/type/spigot/SpigotPluginProvider.java
@@ -118,7 +118,14 @@ public class SpigotPluginProvider implements PluginProvider<JavaPlugin>, Provide
             }
             // Paper end
 
-            server.getUnsafe().checkSupported(this.description);
+            // Lophinya start - folia-supported gate defaults open: this is a second, independent
+            // folia-supported gate that only legacy (Spigot-format) plugins hit, at enable time
+            // rather than discovery time. checkSupported(PluginDescriptionFile) has no jar-path
+            // context, so the allow-list check happens here at the call site instead of inside it.
+            if (!fun.bm.lophinya.compat.LophinyaFoliaSupportedGate.isAllowed(this.path)) {
+                server.getUnsafe().checkSupported(this.description);
+            }
+            // Lophinya end - folia-supported gate defaults open
 
             final PluginClassLoader loader;
             try {
diff --git a/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/plugin/provider/type/spigot/SpigotPluginProviderFactory.java b/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/plugin/provider/type/spigot/SpigotPluginProviderFactory.java
index 8f0b7b2985d3aadaacd5313d52d48ac916d871c9..51117c5813ede0f48c69e76238b9cc0cbab90f15 100644
--- a/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/plugin/provider/type/spigot/SpigotPluginProviderFactory.java
+++ b/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/plugin/provider/type/spigot/SpigotPluginProviderFactory.java
@@ -27,7 +27,8 @@ class SpigotPluginProviderFactory implements PluginTypeFactory<SpigotPluginProvi
     @Override
     public SpigotPluginProvider build(JarFile file, PluginDescriptionFile configuration, Path source) throws InvalidDescriptionException {
         // Folia start - block plugins not marked as supported
-        if (!configuration.isFoliaSupported() && !me.earthme.luminol.config.modules.unsupported.DisableCheckForFoliaSupported.disableForPaper) { // Luminol - disable check for folia supported
+        if (!configuration.isFoliaSupported() && !me.earthme.luminol.config.modules.unsupported.DisableCheckForFoliaSupported.disableForPaper
+            && !fun.bm.lophinya.compat.LophinyaFoliaSupportedGate.isAllowed(source)) { // Lophinya - folia-supported gate defaults open
             throw new RuntimeException("Could not load plugin '" + configuration.getDisplayName() + "' as it is not marked as supporting Folia!");
         }
         // Folia end - block plugins not marked as supported
